          Mario Pascoli
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  "It is a political error to practice deceit, if deceit is carried too 
far."
  -Frederick II, King of Prussia, 1740.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter gave way to sweet spring, and Hokuto made ready to carry out his 
imperial assignments.  Cretacia was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no 
armies in Cretacia.  Hokuto could not cast Flood on Silvermist because 
Mountain terrain is illegal for the Flood spell.  Instead, Hokuto practiced 
his Thievery diligently for many weeks, but could make no progress.
  Starhaven was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 2nd Light Cavalry, 
the 3rd Legion, the 5th Legion, the 172nd Legion, the 192nd Chariots and the 
250th Bowmen in Starhaven and destroyed them.  Cherrywood was hit by a 
plague.  The plague struck the 35th Legion, the 47th Legion, the 113th 
Light Cavalry, the 278th Axemen, the 328th Legion and the 329th Legion in 
Cherrywood and destroyed them.
  With the coming of the early summer season magical tornadoes hit the 
defenders of Starhaven.  The Tornado affected no armies in Starhaven.  
Hokuto moved into Silvermist (#502) with his high-spirited army.
  The plague struck the 71st Legion in Silvermist and destroyed them.  The 
plague struck the 154th Legion in Silvermist and destroyed them.  The plague 
struck the 233rd Chariots in Silvermist and destroyed them.  Amberleaf was 
hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Amberleaf.  Kilkenny was 
hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Kilkenny.
  In late summer, magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Cretacia.  Hokuto 
moved into Cretacia.
  During fall, Hokuto practiced his Element Magic well, and even consulted a 
palm reader, but could not improve his skill in Element Magic.
  With the coming of the early winter season Hokuto practiced his Element 
Magic for months, but could make no significant headway.


  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
entered Cherrywood, hoping to subjugate that province owned by Hokuto and 
made up of great Forests.  Cherrywood was conquered and occupied by Teleko 
(#72)'s host.  Teleko leads approximately 1 Dragons, 5 Eagles and 1 Trolls.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai (#3) (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Hokuto, degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Hokuto for this year.

  Mugai Treated with Hokuto, but Hokuto did not respond favorably to his 
amicable noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will see the wisdom 
of Treating.

  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Attla (#54) has arrived in St Helens from Silvermist.
  Loviatar (#92) hiked into Amberleaf.  She had grown bored with Maicuru and 
was drawn there by tales of its fine wines and even finer courtesans.


  Here is the financial report for Hokuto's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 14 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Hokuto was left with 16 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Mortimer, Squire to Ningarl
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring, and Ningarl prepared to carry out 
his imperial assignments.  He marched on Cherrywood (#501) with his forces.
  With the advent of the early summer season Ningarl moved into Cretacia 
(#601) with his redoubtable army.
  In late summer, tornadoes sucked up the 10th Light Cavalry in Cretacia and 
destroyed them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 112th Bowmen in Cretacia and 
destroyed them.  Ningarl's Bless spell backfired and Ningarl was left 
covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Ningarl was instructed in Element Magic by 
Hokuto.  Ningarl practiced his Element Magic and his skill in Element Magic 
went up.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Mountain province of 
Cretacia, ruled by Hokuto.  Teleko (#72) was in command of the attacking 
armies.  The defenders were led by Ningarl.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Cretacia (0601):

