  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 321st Eagles, the 322nd Eagles and the 326th Dragons 
in reserve.  The defenders had the 330th Chariots in reserve.  Teleko 
commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Ningarl stood ready at the head of his 
thousands.
  Teleko stepped forward and challenged Ningarl to honorable combat.  
Ningarl answered the challenge to honorable combat.  Teleko chanted his 
strange words of magic and cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Ningarl quake 
and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Ningarl speedily moved into bow range.  Teleko chanted his strange words 
of magic and cast a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in the shape of a 
cross formed around Teleko.
  Ningarl closed to melee range, seething with blood-lust.  Showing no fear, 
Ningarl moved closer and swang at Teleko but his aim was just off the mark.  
Teleko's spell was disrupted by the event.  Teleko swang at Ningarl and 
walloped him with 6 damage points.  Ningarl thrust at Teleko and scored 1 
damage points on him.
  Teleko deftly swang at Ningarl and damaged him, inflicting 5 damage 
points.  Ningarl fell, fatally injured.  Thus did Ningarl die, a defiant 
death by any standard.
  The forces commanded by Ningarl were disheartened by his demise, yet still 
they moved forward with some hope of victory.  Teleko's luck wasn't very 
good this time.  His superstitious men became unsettled when his priests 
were unable to properly sacrifice a goat to the gods because they had all 
been stolen by gryphons.  On the other hand tactical superiority was clearly 
guaranteed by Teleko's powerful tactical genius.
  The Dwarves commanded by Ningarl were not impressed by his lack of 
leadership ability.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
216th Axemen, who sang out their battle hymns, inspired with a spirit of 
holy, fanatical fury by their exalted King.  The 323rd Trolls met their 
match against the doughty Axemen, tragically unable to avoid having their 
long legs cut to shreds.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 48th Chariots and 
attacked them.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 227th Light Cavalry and 
attacked them.  The 321st Eagles swooped down on the 330th Chariots and 
attacked without mercy.  The 322nd Eagles soared over the 216th Axemen and 
attacked them.
  Teleko maneuvered the 320th Eagles to the fore, as a strategem for a 
superior nemesis effect.  The 320th Eagles fought with the 216th Axemen and 
cut them down like beanstalks.
  The forces of Teleko broke through the lines of their opposition and were 
victorious.  The 320th Eagles slew the 216th Axemen almost to a man.  The 
323rd Trolls scattered the 48th Chariots in all directions.  The 319th 
Eagles destroyed the 227th Light Cavalry.  The 321st Eagles annihilated the 
330th Chariots.
  Cretacia was overrun by Teleko's men in a hard-fought campaign.  Its 
forces completely destroyed, the acting commander fled alone to Cherrywood.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Ningarl


From: Montgomery, Squire to Lexington
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and Lexington prepared to carry out his 
imperial orders.  He enlisted the 3rd Legion and the 5th Legion in Starhaven 
to serve Lexington.  Lexington couldn't recruit Chariots in Starhaven 
because there wasn't enough gold.
  During early summer, Lexington cast a Bless spell.  Starhaven was 
magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 2nd 
Light Cavalry, the 3rd Legion and the 5th Legion were Blessed and 
permanently destroyed.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  Lexington's 
Bless spell fizzled and Lexington wound up covered with psycho-kinetic goo.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1)'s forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Starhaven, a Forest province owing allegiance to Hokuto.
Teleko (#72) commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by 
Lexington.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Starhaven (0701):

