  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 319th Eagles, the 321st Eagles and the 322nd Eagles 
in reserve.  Teleko stood ready at the head of his thousands.  Lexington 
marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.
  Teleko strode forward and challenged Lexington to personal combat.  
Lexington accepted the challenge to honorable combat.  Teleko incanted his 
strange words of magic and cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Lexington quake 
and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Lexington advanced to bow range.  Waving his hands, Teleko orchestrated 
otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in 
the shape of a cross formed around Teleko.
  Lexington charged into melee range.  Seeking to take advantage of a weak 
point in Teleko's protection, Lexington deftly swang at Teleko but his sword 
whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Raising his hands high in the air, 
Teleko cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with 
his hands.  Lexington then thrust at Teleko and would have hit him if Teleko 
hadn't sidestepped just then.  Teleko seized his neck with unseen hands and 
shook it and scored on Lexington, doing 3 points of damage.
  Lexington thrust at Teleko but his sword whiffed harmlessly through the 
air.  Teleko clenched his fist tightly, squeezing the innards of Lexington 
and inflicted 3 damage points.  Lexington swang at his enemy and missed.  
Teleko brought his hands together and pulled them apart in a tearing motion, 
provoking a blood-curdling squeal from Lexington and damaged him, scoring 3 
damage points.
  Lexington contemptuously thrust at Teleko but his sword whiffed harmlessly 
through the air.  Teleko brought his hands together and yanked them apart in 
a ripping gesture, provoking a squeal of pain from Lexington and inflicted 3 
damage points on him.  Lexington energetically swang at Teleko and missed by 
a mile.  Teleko curled his phantasmal hand around Lexington's liver and 
squeezed it viciously and scorched Lexington with 3 damage points.  
Lexington fell, mortally injured.  Thus did Lexington finally die, a brave 
end by any standard.
  The forces commanded by Lexington were disheartened by his death, but 
still they moved forward with some hope of victory.  As luck would have it, 
Teleko's formations were well hidden by a sudden mist, giving them a small 
edge.  Also, tactical superiority was clearly assured by Teleko's powerful 
tactical genius.
  Hokuto's soldiers were prepared to struggle like tigers for their 
homeland.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 323rd Trolls faced the 191st Legion.  
The 326th Dragons soared over the 191st Legion and attacked them.  The 323rd 
Trolls battled with the 191st Legion and cut them down like weeds.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Hokuto, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the battle for Teleko. 
The 323rd Trolls destroyed the 191st Legion.
  Teleko's campaign effected the conquest of Starhaven.  Its forces 
completely dispersed, the acting commander escaped frightened and alone to 
Kilkenny.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Lexington


